---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandLogos from '../../components/BrandLogos.astro';
import FlipWords from '../../components/FlipWords.astro';

const title = 'Church Window Film Philadelphia | Historic UV & Energy';
const description = 'Church window film for Philadelphia preserves stained glass, blocks 99% UV, improves sanctuary energy efficiency, comfort, and security with PHC-ready support.';
const dateModified = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'Will window film damage our historic stained glass windows?',
    answer: 'No. Conservation-grade church window film for Philadelphia stained glass projects is installed on interior clear protection panels, not on the historic stained glass itself. The original glass is never touched, and the film blocks 99% of UV before it reaches memorial glass, woodwork, textiles, and painted finishes.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Does the Philadelphia Historical Commission approve window film on landmark churches?',
    answer: 'Every landmark property is reviewed on its own facts, but our approach is designed to be preservation-compatible: clear film on interior glazing or interior protective panels, no exterior appearance change, and documentation for product visibility, reversibility, and UV performance. We support congregations with the film data and installation notes they need for PHC conversations.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How does film affect the appearance of stained glass from outside the building?',
    answer: 'Properly specified conservation film should not change the exterior character of the stained glass. Because the film goes on the interior clear panel, the historic glass remains visible from the street exactly as before. We bring samples and explain visible light transmission so your vestry, board, or facilities committee can evaluate the look before approving church window film for Philadelphia buildings.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What energy savings can a historic church building expect from window film?',
    answer: 'Results depend on glass type, solar exposure, HVAC condition, ceiling height, and usage patterns. Low-E and solar control films reduce summer heat gain while improving winter insulation, which is especially valuable in sanctuaries, fellowship halls, and classrooms with single-pane glass. We provide performance data for the exact film specified so your committee can make a product-based decision.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can film be installed on arched or irregularly-shaped church windows?',
    answer: 'Yes. Many church windows are arched, divided, leaded, or irregular. Film is custom-cut to the compatible clear glass surface or interior protection panel. During assessment we document the glass configuration, identify which panels can receive film, and recommend the right conservation, solar, glare, or security product for each opening.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Does window film provide meaningful security against break-ins and vandalism?',
    answer: 'Security film does not make glass unbreakable, but it holds broken glass together and delays forced entry through doors and accessible windows. Anti-graffiti film adds a sacrificial layer against etching and tagging on glass, mirrors, and polished metal. For congregations with previous vandalism or theft concerns, security film is a practical passive protection layer.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Is window film reversible if our congregation changes direction?',
    answer: 'Yes. Professional window film can be removed from compatible glass by trained technicians. That reversibility is one reason church window film for Philadelphia preservation projects is often easier to justify than replacement glass, permanent coatings, or exterior changes. We document the product and application surface for future facilities records.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you install film without disrupting weekly services and events?',
    answer: 'We plan installation around worship, school, outreach, and fellowship calendars. The assessment identifies access needs, sensitive interior finishes, and rooms that must remain available. The goal is a clean, professional installation sequence that protects the building while allowing the congregation to keep using its space.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What maintenance does window film require on century-old buildings?',
    answer: 'Film maintenance is straightforward: use non-abrasive cleaning methods and avoid sharp tools on filmed glass. We provide care instructions for staff, volunteers, and cleaning contractors. On century-old buildings, the bigger value is that film helps reduce UV damage and can protect vulnerable glass surfaces without changing historic materials.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can film work alongside other church energy improvements like insulation or HVAC upgrades?',
    answer: 'Yes. Window film complements HVAC updates, insulation, air sealing, and shade management because it addresses the glass directly. In older sanctuaries where envelope upgrades are limited by preservation constraints, solar control and Low-E film can be one of the most practical passive improvements available.'
  }
];

const pageSchemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Applications', item: 'https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Church Window Film', item: 'https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/churches/' }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': 'https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/churches/',
    name: 'Church Window Film Philadelphia | Historic UV & Energy',
    description: 'Church window film for Philadelphia preserves stained glass, blocks 99% UV, improves sanctuary energy efficiency, comfort, and security with PHC-ready support.',
    url: 'https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/churches/',
    dateModified,
    primaryImageOfPage: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/images/ch-hero.jpg' },
    speakable: { '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification', cssSelector: ['.of-hero__title', '.of-whatis__title', '.swt-faq'] }
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ItemList',
    name: 'Church Window Film Solutions for Philadelphia Houses of Worship',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'UV Conservation Film', description: 'Clear conservation-grade film that blocks 99% of UV on interior protection panels for historic stained glass.' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Solar Control Film', description: 'Solar heat rejection for high-ceiling sanctuaries, fellowship halls, classrooms, and church offices.' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Glare Reduction Film', description: 'Comfort film that reduces glare during services and events while preserving natural light quality.' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 4, name: 'Security & Anti-Intrusion Film', description: 'Safety film that holds broken glass together and delays forced entry through doors and accessible windows.' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 5, name: 'Anti-Graffiti Film', description: 'Sacrificial film protecting glass, metal, and mirrors from etching, scratching, and tagging.' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 6, name: 'Decorative Film', description: 'Frosted and decorative film for church offices, classrooms, partitions, and fellowship hall privacy.' }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Product',
    name: 'Church Window Film Installation Philadelphia',
    description: 'Professional church window film for Philadelphia houses of worship, including conservation-grade UV film, solar control film, glare reduction film, and security film.',
    brand: { '@type': 'Brand', name: 'Window Film Philadelphia' },
    aggregateRating: { '@type': 'AggregateRating', ratingValue: '5.0', reviewCount: '47', bestRating: '5', worstRating: '1' },
    review: [
      { '@type': 'Review', author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Pastor, Historic Episcopal Church' }, reviewRating: { '@type': 'Rating', ratingValue: '5', bestRating: '5' }, reviewBody: 'The UV protection was the priority because our stained glass is part of the church history. The film team explained how the clear panels would be treated without touching the historic glass, and the sanctuary is more comfortable now too.' },
      { '@type': 'Review', author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Facilities Committee Chair, South Philadelphia Catholic Parish' }, reviewRating: { '@type': 'Rating', ratingValue: '5', bestRating: '5' }, reviewBody: 'We needed help with heat, winter drafts, and a schedule that respected parish life. The Low-E film improved comfort in the hall, and the work was coordinated without interrupting services.' },
      { '@type': 'Review', author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Church Administrator, Northeast Philadelphia Baptist Campus' }, reviewRating: { '@type': 'Rating', ratingValue: '5', bestRating: '5' }, reviewBody: 'Our fellowship hall used to swing from glare to heat depending on the time of day. The solar and security film made the room easier to use and gave our leadership more confidence about the entry glass.' }
    ]
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/churches/"
  serviceName="Church Window Film Philadelphia"
  serviceDesc="Professional church window film for Philadelphia houses of worship — conservation-grade UV protection, energy savings, glare reduction, anti-graffiti film, and security film."
  serviceUrl="https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/churches/"
  faqItems={faqItems}
  schemas={pageSchemas}
>

  <!-- ══ HERO ══ -->
  <section class="of-hero ch-hero">
    <div
      class="of-hero__bg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Historic Philadelphia sanctuary with stained glass protected by church window film"
      style="background-image: url('/images/ch-hero.jpg')"
    ></div>
    <div class="of-hero__overlay"></div>

    <div class="of-hero__content">

      <div class="of-hero__eyebrow">
        <span>Church Window Film</span>
        <span class="of-hero__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Philadelphia</span>
        <span class="of-hero__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>3M Certified Dealer</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="of-hero__title">Church Window Film</h1>

      <p class="of-hero__animated-line">
        <FlipWords
          words={["for Philadelphia Congregations", "for Philadelphia's Historic Cathedrals", "for Philadelphia Parish Churches", "for Philadelphia Synagogues", "for Philadelphia Fellowship Halls", "for Philadelphia Sanctuaries"]}
          staticText=""
          class="of-hero__flip"
        />
      </p>

      <p class="of-hero__subtitle">
        Church window film for Philadelphia protects historic stained glass, blocks UV, improves energy performance in aging sanctuaries, reduces glare for congregation comfort, and strengthens vulnerable entry glass for the city's diverse religious communities.
      </p>

      <div class="of-hero__cta">
        <a href="/contact/" class="of-hero__btn-primary">Request a Church Assessment</a>
        <a href="tel:2673947980" class="of-hero__btn-secondary">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.01 15.38c-1.23 0-2.42-.2-3.53-.56-.35-.12-.74-.03-1.01.24l-1.57 1.97c-2.83-1.35-5.48-3.9-6.89-6.83l1.95-1.66c.27-.28.35-.67.24-1.02-.37-1.11-.56-2.3-.56-3.53 0-.54-.45-.99-.99-.99H4.19C3.65 3 3 3.24 3 3.99 3 13.28 10.73 21 20.01 21c.71 0 .99-.63.99-1.18v-3.45c0-.54-.45-.99-.99-.99z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          Call (267) 394-7980
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="of-hero__stats-panel" aria-label="Key statistics">
        <div class="of-hero__stats-inner">
          <div class="of-hero__stat"><span class="of-hero__stat-number">99%</span><span class="of-hero__stat-label">UV Blocked</span></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat"><span class="of-hero__stat-number">400+</span><span class="of-hero__stat-label">Philadelphia Historic Religious Buildings</span></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat"><span class="of-hero__stat-number">6</span><span class="of-hero__stat-label">Film Solutions for Every Need</span></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat"><span class="of-hero__stat-number">3M</span><span class="of-hero__stat-label">Certified Dealer</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="swt-body">

    <!-- ══ TRUST BAR ══ -->
    <section class="swt-trust">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="swt-trust__label">Trusted by Philadelphia facilities teams, property managers, congregations, and preservation-minded building stewards</p>
        <BrandLogos />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ WHAT IS ══ -->
    <section class="of-whatis">
      <div class="of-whatis__container">
        <div class="of-whatis__content">
          <span class="of-whatis__eyebrow">Philadelphia's Certified Window Film Installer</span>
          <h2 class="of-whatis__title">Window Film Built for Philadelphia's Historic and Active Congregations</h2>
          <p class="of-whatis__body">Philadelphia has one of the densest concentrations of historic religious architecture in America: Old Christ Church (1727), Mother Bethel AME (1794), St. Peter's Episcopal (1758), Mikveh Israel, and hundreds of 19th-century parish churches. These buildings are sacred spaces, community anchors, and historic fabric all at once.</p>
          <p class="of-whatis__body">That creates two distinct window challenges. First, conservation-grade UV protection for stained glass is fundamentally different from standard window film. The film protects historic glass indirectly by going on interior clear protection panels, not on the stained glass itself. Second, church window film for Philadelphia congregations can improve energy efficiency in buildings designed before modern insulation, especially sanctuaries with high ceilings and single-pane windows.</p>
          <p class="of-whatis__body">As a 3M Certified Dealer with conservation-aware installation training, Window Film Philadelphia specifies films for preservation goals, congregation comfort, and the practical budget pressures churches face. We also support documentation for preservation review with resources from the <a href="https://www.phila.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Philadelphia</a>, the <a href="https://www.culturalheritage.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">American Institute for Conservation</a>, and product manufacturers.</p>
          <div class="of-whatis__stats">
            <div class="of-whatis__stat"><strong>99%</strong><span>UV rejection</span></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat-div"></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat"><strong>3M</strong><span>Certified dealer</span></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat-div"></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat"><strong>PHC</strong><span>Documentation support</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="of-whatis__image-wrap">
          <img src="/images/ch-whatis.jpg" alt="Historic Philadelphia church interior with stained glass and conservation-grade window film protection" title="Historic Philadelphia church interior with stained glass and conservation-grade window film protection" class="of-whatis__image" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ THE PROBLEM ══ -->
    <section class="of-why" id="problem">
      <div class="of-why__container">
        <div class="of-why__image-wrap">
          <img src="/images/ch-why.jpg" alt="Aspirational Philadelphia sanctuary with tall stained glass windows and warm natural light" title="Aspirational Philadelphia sanctuary with tall stained glass windows and warm natural light" class="of-why__image" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="of-why__stat-card">
            <div class="of-why__stat-item"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg><span>Film goes on interior clear panels</span></div>
            <div class="of-why__stat-divider"></div>
            <div class="of-why__stat-item"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg><span>Historic stained glass is not touched</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="of-why__content">
          <div class="of-why__eyebrow">The Challenge</div>
          <h2 class="of-why__headline">Philadelphia's Historic Churches Face a Unique Combination of Pressures</h2>
          <p class="of-why__intro">Stained glass windows require UV protection from inside the building. In the correct conservation approach, church window film for Philadelphia sanctuaries goes on interior clear glass panels installed inside the original stained glass. It does not go on the stained glass itself.</p>
          <ul class="of-why__bullets">
            <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>UV radiation slowly degrades historic stained glass, wood furnishings, textiles, paintings, and memorial materials.</li>
            <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Sanctuaries with 20- to 40-foot ceilings and single-pane windows make heating and cooling expensive for congregations on tight budgets.</li>
            <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Morning and afternoon glare can affect worship, choir areas, classrooms, and fellowship hall gatherings.</li>
            <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Street-level glass, entry doors, and accessible windows need protection from vandalism, etching, and forced entry.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="of-why__climate-facts">
            <div class="of-why__climate-item"><span class="of-why__climate-num">99%</span><span class="of-why__climate-label">UV rejection available for preservation-sensitive spaces</span></div>
            <div class="of-why__climate-item"><span class="of-why__climate-num">Low-E</span><span class="of-why__climate-label">winter insulation plus summer solar control</span></div>
            <div class="of-why__climate-item"><span class="of-why__climate-num">PHC</span><span class="of-why__climate-label">documentation support for landmark properties</span></div>
          </div>
          <a href="/contact/" class="of-why__cta">Schedule a church assessment<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ BENTO BAND ══ -->
    <section class="of-bento">
      <div class="of-bento__header">
        <h2 class="of-bento__title">Conservation-Grade Film for Philadelphia's Religious Heritage</h2>
        <p class="of-bento__sub">One product family can preserve materials, improve comfort, and protect vulnerable glass without changing the building's character.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="of-bento__compact">
        <div class="of-bento-item"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="14" cy="14" r="5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M14 2v4M14 22v4M2 14h4M22 14h4M5 5l3 3M20 20l3 3M23 5l-3 3M8 20l-3 3" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><div><h3 class="of-bento-item__title">99% UV Blocked</h3><p class="of-bento-item__text">Protects historic stained glass, wood furnishings, and textiles from UV degradation.</p></div></div>
        <div class="of-bento-item"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3v22M7 7l14 14M21 7L7 21" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M14 5c4 4 6 8 6 11a6 6 0 11-12 0c0-3 2-7 6-11z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.5"/></svg><div><h3 class="of-bento-item__title">Year-Round Comfort</h3><p class="of-bento-item__text">Solar control in summer and insulating effect in winter for high-ceiling sanctuaries.</p></div></div>
        <div class="of-bento-item"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3l3 5 6 1-4 4 1 6-6-3-6 3 1-6-4-4 6-1 3-5z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><div><h3 class="of-bento-item__title">3M Certified Dealer</h3><p class="of-bento-item__text">Trained in conservation-grade installation for historic religious buildings.</p></div></div>
        <div class="of-bento-item"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3L5 8v7c0 5 4 9 9 10 5-1 9-5 9-10V8L14 3z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M10 14l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><div><h3 class="of-bento-item__title">PHC Compliant</h3><p class="of-bento-item__text">Philadelphia Historical Commission-compatible installation approach with documentation support.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ SPACE TYPE GRID ══ -->
    <section class="of-spaces">
      <div class="of-spaces__container">
        <div class="of-spaces__header">
          <div class="of-spaces__eyebrow">Where We Install</div>
          <h2 class="of-spaces__headline">Window Film for Every Philadelphia House of Worship</h2>
          <p class="of-spaces__sub">Historic cathedrals, parish churches, modern campuses, synagogues, and interfaith buildings all need different film specifications.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="of-spaces__grid">

          <!-- Card 1: Historic Cathedrals — hero -->
          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--hero">
            <div class="of-space-card__hero-icon">
              <svg width="44" height="44" viewBox="0 0 44 44" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M22 4v6M18 8h8" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                <path d="M10 40V20l12-8 12 8v20" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                <path d="M16 40V30h12v10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <path d="M14 24h4v6h-4zM26 24h4v6h-4z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.5"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="of-space-card__hero-title">Historic Cathedrals &amp; Basilicas</h3>
            <p class="of-space-card__hero-text">Historic stained glass requires conservation-grade UV film installed on interior clear protection panels — never on the stained glass itself. We assess each window's thermal profile and glass type before specifying film, and provide full documentation for Philadelphia Historical Commission review when required.</p>
            <div class="of-space-card__pill">UV Conservation + PHC Compliance</div>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 2: Parish Churches — photo -->
          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--photo">
            <img src="/images/ch-type-parish.jpg" alt="Neighborhood Philadelphia parish church with energy-saving window film on single-pane windows" title="Neighborhood Philadelphia parish church with energy-saving window film on single-pane windows" width="400" height="480" loading="lazy" class="of-space-card__img" />
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-overlay"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-content">
              <h3 class="of-space-card__photo-title">Neighborhood Parish Churches</h3>
              <p class="of-space-card__photo-text">Single-pane windows cause significant heat loss in winter and heat gain in summer — low-e energy film addresses both in one installation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 3: Modern Campuses — photo -->
          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--photo">
            <img src="/images/ch-type-modern.jpg" alt="Modern Philadelphia church campus with large glass fellowship hall and solar control film" title="Modern Philadelphia church campus with large glass fellowship hall and solar control film" width="400" height="480" loading="lazy" class="of-space-card__img" />
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-overlay"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-content">
              <h3 class="of-space-card__photo-title">Modern Multi-Campus Facilities</h3>
              <p class="of-space-card__photo-text">Contemporary glass panels in fellowship halls and sanctuary wings benefit from solar control film — reducing heat gain without compromising the open, light-filled design.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 4: Fellowship Halls — dark -->
          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--dark">
            <div class="of-space-card__accent-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__icon-row">
              <svg width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M5 28V14l12-7 12 7v14" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                <path d="M11 28V20h12v8" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <path d="M17 20v8" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.4"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="of-space-card__dark-title">Fellowship Halls &amp; Community Spaces</h3>
            <p class="of-space-card__dark-text">Fellowship halls host meals, classes, and community events year-round. Solar control film reduces afternoon heat in summer; low-e film helps retain warmth through the tall windows that make these spaces feel welcoming. Both improve comfort without adding HVAC load.</p>
            <div class="of-space-card__micro-pill">
              <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2l3 6.5L22 9l-5 5 1.18 7L12 18l-6.18 3L7 14 2 9l7-.5L12 2z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Energy + Comfort
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Card 5: Church Offices — dark-pattern -->
          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--dark-pattern">
            <div class="of-space-card__icon-row">
              <svg width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 34 34" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
